§§ `11. Disappearance`

-- The insurer treats the insured as dead and pays the death benefit if the insured has
-- disappeared and there is enough evidence to lead the insurer to conclude that the
-- insured suffered a bodily injury that caused death; the payees undertake to repay if the
-- insured is later found alive.
